1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,500
Across the shimmering mirror of the Venetian Lagoon, the Ponte della Libertà stretches four kilometres toward the sea.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Built in 1933 by Eugenio Miozzi, this slender causeway carries the only road connecting the mainland to Venice.

3
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:24,500
To our left and right, historic batteries and wooden briccole guide fishermen through the ancient salt marshes.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:33,000
As the road approaches Santa Chiara, the open lagoon yields to the stone embankments of Cannaregio.

5
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:41,500
Ahead across the Grand Canal, the great copper dome of San Simeon Piccolo rises like a temple above the water.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
At Sant’Andrea della Zirada, fourteenth-century Gothic walls mark the boundary where asphalt ends and Venice begins.

7
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:58,500
Here at Piazzale Roma, every engine falls silent, handing the traveler over to gondolas, bridges, and labyrinthine stone.
